## Outlines (tools/outlines.py → assets/outlines.json)
- Country outlines: johan/world.geo.json, countries.geo.json (public domain),
  https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/johan/world.geo.json@master/countries.geo.json (copy in raw/countries.geo.json).
  Greenland = the «Greenland» feature; Africa = union of the 51 African features (mainland + Madagascar).
- The 14 copies of Greenland are its true-size outline: projected in a spherical Lambert azimuthal equal-area projection about
  its own centre, only moved and turned inside Africa's equal-area plane (area unchanged), then projected back onto the globe.
  Placement by simulated annealing (least overlap, least spill over the coast). With these generalised outlines:
  Greenland 2.19 M km², Africa 30.04 M km² (ratio 13.7); the 14 copies cover 94 % of mainland Africa, overlap each other by
  1.56 M km² (5 % of their area) and spill 1.33 M km² over the coast — a fair picture of «14 Гренландий уместились бы»,
  not an exact tiling (an exact tiling of an irregular shape is impossible).
- The travelling copy (1.25–3.0 s) is Greenland's outline moved by a rotation of the sphere: shape and size unchanged.

